  "term": "ambulatory treatment",
  "definition": "Ambulatory treatment is care provided in a non-hospital setting rather than through admission, and it is described as a less intensive approach than hospitalization. In the source, it is presented as an option for medically stable patients with eating disorders and, in some guidelines, as the preferred setting for many patients.",
